;; Reviewed 2026-10-10 (written by Claude, from design section 15, DCL
;; Dictionary DCL1-5, the LIB$ and System Services manuals, the guest runs
;; and the debugger run; for the user's review). Why this is right:
;; - TEXT holds the arguments, each ended by 0X: 2050 bytes, room for
;;   argument 0 (at most 1024 bytes, POC_IMAGE_NAME's buffer) and the line
;;   (1024) split, each with its 0X. STARTS holds where each starts: 513
;;   INTEGERs, as each argument after 0 takes a character and a blank but
;;   the last. ArgCount is exported, a global symbol ("::").
;; - The initializer calls Split. Split has POC_IMAGE_NAME put argument 0
;;   ($GETJPI's JPI$_IMAGNAME) in LINE, its length back in R0, and copies
;;   it to the start of TEXT with its 0X; ArgCount is 1. Then POC_FOREIGN
;;   puts LIB$GET_FOREIGN's line in LINE ("" when the image was not run
;;   as a foreign command).
;; - Split's loop skips blanks (32 and 9), stops at the line's end, and
;;   records where the next argument starts and counts it. Then, until a
;;   blank outside quotes or the end: a character other than " (34) is
;;   copied; "" inside quotes is copied as one "; any other " toggles
;;   quoted (XORB2 #1) and is dropped. Then the argument's 0X. Every index
;;   is checked against its array (trap 2), as poc's range checks always
;;   are.
;; - GetArg returns at once for an array of length 0; else it copies
;;   argument n, if 0 <= n < ArgCount (CMPW, words under -O2), from
;;   TEXT[STARTS[n]] up to its 0X or LEN(val) - 1 characters, and ends val
;;   with 0X, which makes val "" for any other n.
;; - On the guest, ArgsOut run as a foreign command with
;;   -o "Hello"  mixedCase a"b"c "x""y" "" "two  spaces"<TAB>tab prints
;;   -O, Hello, MIXEDCASE, AbC, x"y, "", two  spaces and TAB, under -O2
;;   and -OC; run by RUN, it has argument 0 alone (guest-run.expected).
; Modules, written by poc (doc/developer/vax-macro32-backend.md)
